<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">submit</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">submit</ansi> command forces a grappled opponent to yield. You must
be in control of a grounded grapple to attempt it. It's a special
move — it shares the combat cooldown with <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>, and <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">submit</ansi>              Force your grappled opponent to yield.

<ansi fg="yellow">Outcomes: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="green">Yield</ansi>     — the opponent submits and combat ends.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Resist</ansi>    — the opponent refuses; you wrench them for damage.
  <ansi fg="red">Failure</ansi>    — you overcommit and fall to the ground.

Wounded player opponents are more likely to yield. Mobs always
resist. The attempt progresses your Unarmed Combat skill.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help grapple</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help attack</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help flee</ansi>
